rd":3.3,"div_yield":3.21,"ps_ratio":2.4,"fcf_to_ev":3.15,"fcf_to_mcap":10.46,"liab_to_assets":66,"cash_to_assets":4.3,"current_ratio":0.98,"roe":14.4,"roa":4.9,"moat":{"ticker":"ELC","period":"2026Q2","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"ELC 作為受監管的公用事業公司，其品牌和定價權受到嚴格的監管機構審查。公司無法自由設定價格以反映其品牌價值或市場需求，而是依賴於批准的費率結構。因此，在品牌定價權方面，其護城河極為薄弱，幾乎不存在獨立定價的能力，這與巴菲特所青睞的擁有強大定價權的消費品牌截然不同。","comment_en":"As a regulated utility, Entergy Louisiana, LLC (ELC) faces significant regulatory oversight on its branding and pricing power. The company cannot freely set prices to reflect brand value or market demand, relying instead on approved rate structures. Consequently, its moat in brand pricing is extremely weak, with virtually no independent pricing capability, unlike consumer brands with strong pricing power favored by Buffett."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"ELC 的核心護城河來自其受監管的公用事業特許經營權。這意味著其在特定地理區域內提供電力服務擁有獨家或近乎獨家的權利，並受到政府監管機構的批准。這種特許經營權是進入壁壘極高的天然壟斷，有效阻止了競爭對手的進入，為公司提供了穩定的收入來源和可預測的利潤率。","comment_en":"ELC's primary moat stems from its regulated utility franchise. This grants it exclusive or near-exclusive rights to provide electricity services within specific geographic areas, subject to regulatory approval. These franchises represent extremely high barriers to entry, effectively preventing competitors and providing the company with a stable revenue stream and predictable profit margins."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"對於電力消費者而言，轉換電力供應商的成本非常高。基礎設施（電線、變電站）是固定的，且用戶通常無法選擇不同的電力網絡。即使有零售電力市場，更換供應商的過程也涉及複雜的程序和潛在的服務中斷風險，使得絕大多數用戶傾向於維持現狀，為 ELC 提供了穩定的客戶基礎。","comment_en":"For electricity consumers, the costs of switching power providers are prohibitively high. The underlying infrastructure (wires, substations) is fixed, and end-users typically cannot choose different electrical grids. Even in competitive retail markets, the process of changing suppliers involves complex procedures and potential service disruption risks, leading the vast majority of users to maintain their current provider, securing a stable customer base for ELC."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":1,"comment_zh":"ELC 的業務模式不具備顯著的網絡效應。其電力傳輸和配電網絡的價值主要取決於其物理基礎設施的覆蓋範圍和效率，而非用戶數量的增加帶來的邊際效用遞增。雖然更多的用戶可以增加總體收入，但這並不會像社交網絡或市場平台那樣，讓網絡本身變得更有價值。","comment_en":"ELC's business model does not exhibit significant network effects. The value of its electricity transmission and distribution network is primarily derived from the reach and efficiency of its physical infrastructure, not from increasing marginal utility as the number of users grows. While more customers increase overall revenue, it doesn't make the network itself more valuable in the way social networks or marketplaces do."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"作為一家大型公用事業公司，ELC 受益於規模經濟。其龐大的基礎設施網絡、集中採購能力以及營運效率，使其單位營運成本低於潛在的小型競爭者。此外，監管框架通常也傾向於認可較大、較有效率的營運商，這進一步鞏固了其成本優勢。","comment_en":"As a large utility, ELC benefits from economies of scale. Its extensive infrastructure network, centralized procurement capabilities, and operational efficiencies result in lower per-unit operating costs compared to potential smaller competitors. Furthermore, the regulatory framework often favors larger, more efficient operators, reinforcing its cost advantage."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":9,"comment_zh":"ELC 在路易斯安那州特定區域的電力基礎設施（發電廠、輸配電網絡）是其獨特的地理資產。這些資產是建立和維護的成本極高，且受到嚴格的監管批准，使得任何新的進入者都難以複製。這些資產是其提供服務的物理基礎，構成了強大的地理壁壘。","comment_en":"ELC's electricity infrastructure (power plants, transmission and distribution networks) within specific regions of Louisiana constitutes its unique geographic assets. These assets are extremely costly to build and maintain, and their operation requires stringent regulatory approvals, making them nearly impossible for new entrants to replicate. These physical assets are fundamental to its service provision and form a formidable geographic barrier."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"公用事業行業高度依賴營運效率來維持盈利能力，尤其是在受到嚴格監管的情況下。ELC 通過優化其發電、輸配電和維護流程，以及利用技術升級來提高效率。雖然監管機構會審查其效率，但持續的營運改進仍能為公司帶來相對穩定的利潤率。","comment_en":"The utility sector relies heavily on operational efficiency to maintain profitability, especially under strict regulation. ELC strives for efficiency by optimizing its generation, transmission, distribution, and maintenance processes, alongside technological upgrades. While regulators scrutinize efficiency, continuous operational improvements can still yield relatively stable profit margins for the company."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"ELC 的資本配置主要集中在維護和升級現有基礎設施，以及進行符合監管批准的投資。雖然其資本配置相對穩定且可預測，但相較於擁有廣泛併購或股票回購機會的企業，其靈活性和創造超額回報的潛力較低。其 ROE 14.4% 顯示了尚可的資本回報率。","comment_en":"ELC's capital allocation is primarily focused on maintaining and upgrading existing infrastructure and making investments approved by regulators. While its allocation is relatively stable and predictable, its flexibility and potential for generating excess returns are lower compared to companies with broad M&A or share buyback opportunities. Its ROE of 14.4% indicates a decent return on capital."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"如轉換成本所述，ELC 在其服務區域內享有極高的客戶保留率。由於電力是基本必需品，且更換供應商的障礙很高，大多數客戶會持續使用 ELC 的服務。這種穩定的客戶基礎為公司提供了可靠的收入來源，是其護城河的重要組成部分。","comment_en":"As noted under switching costs, ELC enjoys extremely high customer retention within its service territory. Electricity is a basic necessity, and the barriers to changing providers are significant, ensuring most customers continue using ELC's services. This stable customer base provides a reliable revenue stream, forming a crucial part of its moat."},"m10_durability":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"ELC 的業務具有高度的持久性。作為提供基礎電力服務的公用事業公司，其需求相對穩定，不易受經濟週期波動的影響。監管框架雖然限制了增長，但也提供了穩定性。只要社會對電力有持續需求，ELC 的業務就能長期持續下去。","comment_en":"ELC's business possesses high durability. As a utility providing essential electricity services, its demand is relatively stable and less susceptible to economic cycles. While the regulatory framework limits growth, it also provides stability. As long as society requires electricity, ELC's business is positioned for long-term continuation."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"Entergy Louisiana, LLC (ELC) 的經濟護城河主要建立在其受監管的公用事業特許經營權（M2）和獨特的地理資產（M6）之上，這構成了極高的進入壁壘，使其在特定區域內享有天然壟斷地位。高轉換成本（M3）和穩定的客戶基礎（M9）進一步鞏固了其市場地位。規模經濟（M5）和營運效率（M7）也提供了成本優勢。然而，其品牌定價權（M1）和網絡效應（M4）極為薄弱。資本配置（M8）相對保守，持久性（M10）良好。總體而言，ELC 屬於典型的「收費橋」或「特許經營」型企業，其護城河的強度主要依賴於監管環境和基礎設施的不可替代性，而非市場競爭優勢。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"Entergy Louisiana, LLC (ELC) possesses a moat primarily built upon its regulated utility franchise (M2) and unique geographic assets (M6), creating formidable barriers to entry and establishing a natural monopoly in its service areas. High switching costs (M3) and stable customer retention (M9) further solidify its market position. Economies of scale (M5) and operational efficiencies (M7) also contribute to its cost advantages. However, its brand pricing power (M1) and network effects (M4) are extremely weak. Capital allocation (M8) is conservative, and durability (M10) is strong. Overall, ELC fits the profile of a 'toll bridge' or 'franchise' business, where its moat strength relies heavily on the regulatory environment and the indispensability of its infrastructure rather than competitive market advantages.","evidenceHash":"df207f390980b0e7a83d81e6d6da8e9d54acaa5ec4de8d74e793723d69eb22b8","assessmentPolicy":"us-buffett-moat-v3"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null},"fScore":{"score":5,"checkedAt":null}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/ELC.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/ELC.png","website":"https://www.entergy.com","ceo":"Drew Marsh","full_time_employees":"12233","description":"Entergy Louisiana LLC operates as an energy utility, focusing on the generation and delivery of electricity. The company also extends its services to include natural gas provision. Its primary corporate offices are located in Jefferson, Louisiana.","description_en":"Entergy Louisiana LLC operates as an energy utility, focusing on the generation and delivery of electricity. The company also extends its services to include natural gas provision. Its primary corporate offices are located in Jefferson, Louisiana.","description_zh":"**Entergy Louisiana, LLC (ELC) 業務營運概述**\n\nEntergy Louisiana, LLC (ELC) 是一家領先的能源公用事業公司，專注於電力之發電與輸配業務。其核心業務涵蓋多元化的發電組合，包括但不限於燃煤、燃氣、核能及再生能源（如太陽能與風力），以確保穩定可靠的電力供應。\n\n除了電力業務，ELC 同時提供天然氣配送服務，滿足客戶多樣化的能源需求。公司透過其廣泛的輸配電網絡，將電力與天然氣安全有效地送達路易斯安那州廣大地區的住宅、商業及工業客戶。\n\nELC 的營運模式強調效率與永續性，持續投資於電網現代化與智慧電網技術，以提升營運韌性、降低損耗並整合更多再生能源。公司致力於提供安全、可靠且具成本效益的能源解決方案，同時積極推動環境保護與社區發展。其主要企業辦公室設於路易斯安那州傑佛遜郡。","address":"639 Loyola Avenue","city":"Jefferson","state":"LA","zip":"70121","country":"US","phone":"+1 504 576 4000","full_address":"639 Loyola Avenue, Jefferson, LA 70121, US","range_52w":"18.05-21.79","year_high":21.79,"year_low":18.05,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":18.05,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[],"stock_splits":[],"fmp_symbol":"ELC","real_5y_prices":[],"historical_dcf_series":[],"name_en":"Entergy Louisiana, LLC COLLATERAL TR MT","expansion":{"status":"available","capturedAt":"2026-10-22T13:21:32.204Z","reason":null,"detailPath":"cache/us_companies/ELC.json"}},"snapshot":null,"model":null}
